<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73355" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὄλυμπος</span></b> , ὁ, 
			Ep.
		 also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Οὔλυμπος</span></b> ,
		metri gr., Mount <u>Olympus</u> (in Thessaly, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			1.56
		</span></i>, etc.), conceived to be the seat of the gods, <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			6.42
		</span></i>, but distd. from heaven (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐρανός</span>),
			<i><span class="en">
			Il.
			15.192
		</span></i> sq., cf. <i><span class="en">
			5.867
		</span></i> sq. ; <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐρανὸς Οὔ. τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					5.750
				</span></i>
			 (but 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐρανός</span>
			, <i>sky,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				20.103
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				113
			</span></i>) ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κρονίωνα θεῶν ἄτερ ἥμενον ἄλλων
					ἀκροτάτῃ κορυφῇ πολυδειράδος Οὐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.754
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑκάστῳ</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶν</span>) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δώματα καλὰ τέτυκτο κατὰ πτύχας
					Οὐλύμποιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.77
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				18.186
			</span></i> : in 
				Att.
			
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐρανός</span>
			, a form of oath, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ τὸν Ὄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OT</u>
					1088
				</span></i>
			
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ant.</u>
				758
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of other
			mountains, as in Mysia, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.36
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				522
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				11.1
			</span></i> ; in Laconia, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				2.65.8
			</span></i> ; in Elis, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				8.3.31
			</span></i> ; in Lycia, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				14.3.8
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				14.5.7
			</span></i> ; in Cyprus, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				14.6.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὄλυμπόνδε,</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Οὔλυμπόνδε</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.221
			</span></i>, al. :—<i>to, towards Olympus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				3.36
			</span></i>, etc. ; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Οὐλυμπόθεν</span></b> , <i>from O.,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.214
			</span></i>.</div>
